I commented on and closed one issue, #1073. I skipped the other 11 because no work landed on them this session. Build status is passing.

#1073 (sub-agent spend in the usage record and `/cost`): closed. Commit f41e50fe covers what the earlier comments listed as still open:
• `--output-format json`: the output now has a separate sub_agents object when the run handed work to a sub-agent. A run that didn't is byte-identical to before.
• `--cost-warn`: the warning total now includes sub-agent spend. Spend that couldn't be priced is counted as unpriced, never as $0.
• `/tokens`: now shows the same sub-agent lines /cost already had.
• Trajectory spend sums: extract_trajectory.py now adds sub-agent cost to each phase's total, and the line saying "these sums leave out sub-agent spend" was reworded to match.

Two things to know about this one:
• I closed it even though one place still shows only the parent's spend. That's the per-turn breakdown in /cost. I said in the comment that this is deliberate: those rows are the parent's own turns, sub-agent spend is already on its own lines with a total, and the docs say so. The earlier commit called this a remaining gap ("Part of"); the follow-up commit, which only adds a risk-log line, says "Fixes". I settled that inconsistency by closing the issue and recording the decision.
• It would have auto-closed anyway. The session's 7 commits haven't been pushed yet, and the "Fixes #1073" message closes the issue once it reaches main. So the close couldn't have stayed open without editing commits, which I couldn't do in this phase.

